0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; Beginning of file FPL
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; Floating point stuff...including basic stuff like the four math
0CB9|                       ;   functions, fix, and float; and much more esoteric stuff, like
0CB9|                       ;   transcendental functions.  All routines of any general interest
0CB9|                       ;   are callable.
0CB9|                       ; Hopefully in the near future there will be an arithmetic vector table,
0CB9|                       ;   so you people adding assembly procedures to your system will
0CB9|                       ;   be able to make use of all this wonderful software.
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; Naming conventions used throughout the floating point package...
0CB9|                       ;   FPCa        Floating point constant a.
0CB9|                       ;   FPMa        Floating point macro a.  Some of these macros leave
0CB9|                       ;               well-specified stuff in registers.
0CB9|                       ;   FPFa        Floating point function a.  Takes argument(s) on tos,
0CB9|                       ;               leaves result on tos, and also in EDCB (except for
0CB9|                       ;               FPFFIX, FPFDOUB, FPFHALV).
0CB9|                       ;   FPLa        Floating point low level function.  Not necessarily
0CB9|                       ;               directly callable, and probably not of interest to
0CB9|                       ;               the user.
0CB9|                       ;   FPGa        Floating point global variable a.
0CB9|                       ;   aLb         Floating point local variable b for function a.
0CB9|                       ;   FPRa        Floating point relational function a.  Returns
0CB9|                       ;               Z = false, NZ = true (not yet meaningful).
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ;***************** BASIC FLOATING POINT ARITHMETIC *************;
0CB9|                       ;       Based on an 8080 floating point package by John Lamping
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; Numbers are four byte quantities represented as...
0CB9|                       ; [exp] [sabc v] [w x] [y z]
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; s, a, b, c are bits, v, w, x, y, z are hex digits.
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; Exponent is biased by 128.  Mantissa is always normalized, and includes
0CB9|                       ;   "invisible" bit just in front of a.
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; If exp = 0, number value is zero.
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; number value = (1-2*s) * .1abcvwxyz * 2^(exp-128)
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; Currently only simple rounding is used...true rounding to be implemented
0CB9|                       ;    sometime in the future.
0CB9|                       
PAGE -  48  INTERP    FILE: FPL.TEXT   


0CB9|                       ; Any operation causing overflow or underflow will store a 01H into (FPERROR)
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       ; (I know error handling in these low-level routines could be simplified,
0CB9|                       ;  but error-protocol was changed after this stuff was adapted to be
0CB9|                       ;  used in the P-machine, and it was easier to put in small fixes.)
0CB9|                       
0CB9|                       
